{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 PARTICIPANT THINK-ALOUD TRANSCRIPT\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Assignment:} CCA3 \u8211- Comparative UX Evaluation\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Participant Name:} Omkar Varpe\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Website:} Tractor Research Website\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Testing Method:} Think-Aloud Usability Testing\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 1. Overall Experience\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 I visited the website and found its overall concept very useful for farmers who want to explore available tractor options.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 2. Issues and Suggestions\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 One problem I noticed is that users may have to explore several sections before reaching the information they need. Making the main actions, such as finding tractors, checking prices, and comparing models, more prominent would improve navigation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 3. Positive Aspects\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 What I liked most is that the website focuses on helping users research tractors instead of simply displaying products. I also liked the visual presentation of the tractor listings and the ability to access important details.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4. Overall Feedback\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Overall, the website has good potential to make tractor research easier. A more direct path to the main features would make the website even more user-friendly.\par}
}
